( '6.2', 'CASE 6.2.037', 'Profit Versus Cash Flow', 'Analyze which section of the cash flow statement reflects cash movements from core trading activities. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['Cash flow from operating activities reflects cash movements arising from the core trading activities of a business during the period.', 'The depreciation that a hotel chain charges on its kitchen equipment each year is a cash expense that directly reduces its bank balance at the time it is recorded.', 'Cash flow from investing activities reflects cash movements arising from buying or selling long-term assets during the period.', 'Land owned by a software developer is depreciated in exactly the same way as its office computer equipment, because all fixed assets wear out identically through use.', 'Cash flow from financing activities reflects cash movements arising from borrowing, repaying loans, raising share capital or paying dividends during the period.'], ARRAY[true, false, true, false, true], ARRAY['TRUE — Evaluated against the textbook standard, this assertion is correct. Cash flow from operating activities reflects cash movements arising from the core trading activities of a business during the period.

