( '6.2', 'CASE 6.2.119', 'Depreciation Charge Consistency', 'Analyze why a business purchasing new equipment often shows a negative investing cash flow in that year. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['Depreciation reflects the gradual wearing out of a fixed asset as it is used to help generate revenue over its useful life.', 'Turnover for the year is reported in the balance sheet rather than in the statement of profit and loss.', 'Depreciation has nothing to do with the wearing out of a fixed asset and is simply an arbitrary entry with no economic meaning.', 'If a fixed asset were never depreciated, it would remain on the accounts at its original cost even after years of productive use, overstating its true worth.', 'Depreciation is charged as an expense in the statement of profit and loss without itself requiring a fresh cash payment in the year it is recorded.'], ARRAY[true, false, false, true, true], ARRAY['TRUE — The claim is correct. Depreciation reflects the gradual wearing out of a fixed asset as it is used to help generate revenue over its useful life.

