Apply the case evidence: Distinguishing expenditure from expense explains gaps between cash outflow and reported expense in a year. Check whether the direction of change (higher/lower, above/below the threshold) matches what the statement asserts.

The reasoning chain is complete, so mark the statement true.', 'FALSE — The claim is false. Gross profit is arrived at by deducting all operating expenses, including distribution and administrative costs, from revenue.

